From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-08-18
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] bin/run: guard the SIGHUP registration on Windows

signal.SIGHUP does not exist on Windows, so `signal.signal(signal.SIGHUP, ...)`
raises AttributeError before the handler is installed. The call site sits inside
runClient()'s broad `except Exception` startup path, so the exception is
swallowed and the node exits immediately AFTER its coin daemons have already
been spawned -- leaving orphaned particld / litecoind / monerod processes and no
BasicSwap parent to reap them. On Windows the node "starts and then vanishes".

Gate the registration on `os.name != "nt"`. SIGINT and SIGTERM exist on Windows
and stay unconditional, so Ctrl-C / terminate handling is unchanged.

No-op on every POSIX platform. Upstream-PR candidate; the operator elected to
submit this one.

Applies to: basicswap v0.18.5 (3859612035f8c4476b5cadedf36b875d2f2def5b)
Marker in patched source: PWNDA-PATCH-1
---
 basicswap/bin/run.py | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/basicswap/bin/run.py b/basicswap/bin/run.py
index 696b533..c013df3 100755
--- a/basicswap/bin/run.py
+++ b/basicswap/bin/run.py
@@ -603,7 +603,11 @@ def runClient(
 
         signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, signal_handler)
         signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, signal_handler)
-        signal.signal(signal.SIGHUP, signal_handler)
+        # PWNDA-PATCH-1: SIGHUP does not exist on Windows; the bare registration
+        # raises AttributeError, which the broad except below swallows, killing the
+        # node immediately after its daemons start. Upstream-PR candidate.
+        if os.name != "nt":
+            signal.signal(signal.SIGHUP, signal_handler)
 
         if len(start_only_coins) > 0:
             logger.info(
